WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.933
The Software Factory cards describe a worker writing tests and code before handoff.

2
00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:11.833
Under the proposed separation, those self-tests must not be the sole basis for acceptance.

3
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:15.067
A separate Scrutiny Validator reads the code.

4
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:22.233
A separate User-Testing Validator checks the running application against the contract without reading the source.

5
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:29.600
If a button does not produce the effect required by the contract, passing self-tests does not establish acceptance.

6
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.700
That is a contract-checking example, not proof that dual validation prevents every failure.

7
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:41.233
The cards leave the definition of done for long, open-ended tasks unresolved.
